<title>UK: Sema shares dip as Kleinwort downgrades.</title>
<headline>Sema shares dip as Kleinwort downgrades.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Sema Group Plc dipped on Monday as analysts at Dresdner Kleinwort Benson Plc cut the computer services group to &quot;hold&quot; from &quot;buy,&quot; dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1129 GMT the stock was down 9p at 12.87-1/2 in thin trade of 60,669 shares.</p>
<p>Analysts at Klweinwort were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
</text>
